\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Christian, seek not Yet Repose;
\par Cast thy dreams of ease away;
\par Thou art in the midst of foes:
\par                      Watch and pray.
\par 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Principalities adn powers,
\par Mustering their unseen array,
\par Wait for thy unguarded hours:
\par                      Watch and pray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Gird thy heavenly armour  on;
\par Wear it ever, night and day;
\par Ambushed lies the evil one:
\par                      Watch and pray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Hear the victors who o'ercame;
\par Still they mark each warrior's way;
\par All with one sweet voice exclaim,
\par                      Watch and pray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Hear, above all, hear thy Lord,
\par Him thou lovest to obey;
\par Hide within thy heart His word:
\par                      Watch and pray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Watch, as if on that alone
\par Hung the issue of the day:
\par Pray, that help may be sent down:
\par                      Watch and pray.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

